Job Description
We are looking for a skilled HR Assistant who will support the Human Resources Department mainly with Payroll Administration, Documentation and Database Procedures for employees.
We also expect the person to have requisite knowledge of various other HR functions.
Responsibilities
Coordinate payroll administration Support the development and implementation of HR initiatives and systems;
Provide counseling on policies and procedures;
Be actively involved in recruitment by preparing job descriptions, posting ads and managing the hiring process;
Create and implement effective onboarding plans;
Develop training and development programs;
Assist in performance management processes;
Support the management of disciplinary and grievance issues;
Maintain employee records (attendance, EEO data etc.) according to policy and legal requirements;
Review employment and working conditions to ensure legal compliance.
Qualifications, Skills & Competencies
B.Sc in Human Resources (HR) or related discipline;
2 years relevant experience;
Professional HR certification would be an added advantage;
Strong knowledge of Payroll systems;
Excellent knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite;
Good interpersonal skills;
Strong ability for corporate writing;
Extremely energetic and able to work long hours.
Remuneration
Competitive based on experience.

Job Description
We are currently in need of an Executive Members, who will contribute his/her time, skills and knowledge through being part of the executive member for the growth and benefits of the less vulnerable populace. Our members is derive from diverse social, ethnic and religious backgrounds in Africa. Our members are selected within the Sub-Sahara Africa communities to collaborating together – sharing expertise around the network, working on international advocacy campaigns and developing global partnerships with our supporters.
Responsibilities
Designed a project ideas for the development of his/her communities or any part of the communities in Sub Sahara Africa.
Responsible for the implementation and management of the project designs;
Knowing and understanding an organization’s purpose and mission statement;
Being able to provide people with general information about the NGO’s program and its activities;
Counseling (when necessary) and supporting the Programme Coordinator in the progress of the organization;
Advising the Programme Coordinator about the advantages of partnerships if you are knowledgeable about and/ or part of another organization;
Participating actively in fundraising (i.e writing letters, soliciting, planning events) ;
Support project partners to follow appropriate means, serve as the main contact person for any projects in your neighbourhood. Identify capacity gap and training needs.
Roles
Liaises with the Programme Coordinator to agree on the project implementation strategies plan annual work plans;
Provide monthly narrative and financial reports for the project and work plans;
Implement the project’s Monitoring and Evaluation plan through regular and prompt collection of data and reporting, providing monthly updates as per the project's M&E matrix;
Work with the Programme Coordinator to explore opportunities for the source of fund for the project implementation;
Carry out other duties related to the position of Project officer as requested by the Programme Coordinator.
Overall responsibility for the high quality implementation of project activities;
Specifically these duties include:
Develop relationships with local and regional government authorities; civil society leaders and the formal and informal private sector to encourage their support for the project;
Organisation and facilitation of functional skills workshops and post training support;
Development and implementation of a training programme for local government:
Development of a communications strategy and the implementation of awareness-raising, civic education and advocacy training and support activities.
Requirements
Relevant degree qualification in Development or related fields
Strong organizational management and planning skills
Excellent analytical, report writing
Experience in cooperating with local organisations/ capacity building
Experience in working with communities
Proposal development experience and strong understanding of the communities development
Very flexible and with a positive attitude
Dynamic and willing to take initiative to complete tasks assigned
Excellent knowledge of English written and spoken
Must have strong knowledge and passion for the community and development
Excellent attention to details and time management.
Strong communication and problem solving skill.

