Job Description:
Requirements
Minimum of 5 years verifiable and demonstrable experience in origination and underwriting credit;
Independent judgment with strong analytical, risk sensing, risk assessment and mitigation skills;
Proficiency in reading/interpreting financial and non-financial information for underwriting credit;
A wide latitude of creativity in credit structuring, monitoring, follow up and recovery;
Excellent communication/presentation skills and attitude necessary to establish and maintain positive working relationships with team members;
Vast understanding of the credit business environment and macro-economic dynamics;
A Bachelor’s degree or higher qualifications in a numerate discipline.

JOB OVERVIEW
The Finance Manager is responsible for the financial health of the Company, business analysis, producing financial reports and developing strategies based on financial research. Also responsible for guiding management in financial decision making to ensure the business is financially successful in line with the organization goals, objectives, mission, vision, and values.
ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS
Oversee the day-to-day financial operations within the company and directs corporate financial planning and structure;
Oversee financial department employees, including financial assistants and accountants;
