Key Responsibilities
The Bakery Operations Manager oversees all staff, budgets, and operations of the business.
Manages and oversees the daily operations of the company;
Coordinates daily activities and facilitates communication between employees;
Manages and oversees the activities of the customer service personnel, decorators, bakers, drivers, and other support staff;
Handles external and internal communication of the company;
Manages calendar, prepares for key events, and ensures events run smoothly; Attends business meetings, events, and functions on behalf of the Head Chef;
Ensures the quality of the company’s products- cakes, pastries, and desserts are met; Promotes and markets the company’s products;
Oversees customer’s orders from the point of order to the point of delivery or collection;
Manages calls, resolves client complaints, and other external issues directed from the customer service personnel;
Recommends strategies and advises the Head Chef on issues that pertain to the development of the company;
Liaises with IT professionals to ensure company invoice software is up to date; Delegates tasks to other employees;
Performs other duties as assigned by the Head Chef.
